# Bugs in icpx

- icpx invokes clang-offload-bundler with `-type=cpp` which is not a valid
  type. The proper type would be `ii`, so `-type=ii`.

- Usually build2 generates foo.so.ii during extraction of header dependencies
  (using the C preprocessor) and then uses this file as input to compilation
  instead of foo.cpp. However icpx fails complaining about the redefinition of
  symbols (structs, functions, etc.) which it itself put in there (via
  clang-offload-bundler).

@@ TODO Elaborate on the above.

Currently we work around this by modfying build2 to not pass -fsycl during the
header extraction phase. Here is the patch against the current master:

diff --git a/libbuild2/cc/compile-rule.cxx b/libbuild2/cc/compile-rule.cxx
index 1ff8ea9b..21447ee3 100644
--- a/libbuild2/cc/compile-rule.cxx
+++ b/libbuild2/cc/compile-rule.cxx
@@ -34,6 +34,16 @@ using namespace butl;
 
 namespace build2
 {
+  static void rm_sycl (cstrings& args)
+  {
+    for (auto i{args.begin ()}; i != args.end (); ++i) {
+      if (strcmp (*i, "-fsycl") == 0) {
+        args.erase (i);
+        return;
+      }
+    }
+  }
+
   namespace cc
   {
     using namespace bin;
@@ -3920,6 +3930,8 @@ namespace build2
           append_options (args, t, c_coptions, werror);
           append_options (args, t, x_coptions, werror);
 
+          rm_sycl (args);
+
           switch (cclass)
           {
           case compiler_class::msvc:
@@ -5475,6 +5487,8 @@ namespace build2
           append_options (args, t, c_coptions, werror);
           append_options (args, t, x_coptions, werror);
 
+          rm_sycl (args);
+
